<title>FRANCE: Algeria assessing 150,000T US/Canada durum offers.</title>
<headline>Algeria assessing 150,000T US/Canada durum offers.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria is currently working on a tender to import 150,000 tonnes of U.S and/or Canadian durum wheat, European grain traders said.</p>
<p>The wheat is for shipment in December, January and February, they said.</p>
<p>Algeria, which launched the tender on November 7, is currently reviewing bids placed by exporters, traders said.</p>
<p>Details of the tender break down as follows.</p>
<p>    Tonnage		Shipment date</p>
<p>    50,000 tonnes	December 16-31</p>
<p>    25,000 tonnes	First half January</p>
<p>    25,000 tonnes	Second half January</p>
<p>    25,000 tonnes	February 1-15</p>
<p>    25,000 tonnes	February 15-28</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
